▶ How to run this app, in order
  1. cd into this folder (2.1-Level-1-Simple-DB-Authentication)
  2. npm install                      - install dependencies (once)
  3. cp config.env.example config.env - or let ../0-Atlas-Setup-Automation write it for you
  4. edit config.env                  - set DATABASE (local MongoDB or Atlas)
  5. npm run seed                     - load sample users and games
  6. npm start                        - start the server
  7. open http://localhost:4001/api-docs - try the API in Swagger UI
  8. npm test                         - run the tests (in-memory MongoDB, no setup needed)

▶ What to submit
  1. Exercise every endpoint for Level 1 (the CLO list below says which).
  2. Stop the server with Ctrl+C - the CLO summary is written on shutdown.
  3. Submit the newest file in logs/ (logs/app-latest.log is a copy of it).
  4. A log that shows missing CLOs, or no student name, will be returned unmarked.

▶ Course Learning Outcomes to demonstrate (Level 1)
  L1-CLO1  Connect an Express API to MongoDB using configuration held outside the code
    ·       how: Start the app with a working DATABASE in .env: npm start
  L1-CLO2  Register a user and store the password as a bcrypt hash, never in plain text
    ·       how: POST /api/v1/users/signup with name, email, password, passwordConfirmation
  L1-CLO3  Authenticate a user by comparing a supplied password with the stored hash
    ·       how: POST /api/v1/users/login with a correct email and password
  L1-CLO4  Reject invalid credentials without revealing which part was wrong
    ·       how: POST /api/v1/users/login with a deliberately wrong password
  L1-CLO5  Validate input and report failures with the correct HTTP status code
    ·       how: POST /api/v1/users/signup twice with the same email (409), or with a 3-character password (400)
  L1-CLO6  Implement REST CRUD over a MongoDB collection
    ·       how: Create, list, edit and delete a game: POST, GET, PATCH, DELETE /api/v1/games
  L1-CLO7  Create and manage score records through the API
    ·       how: POST /api/v1/scores three times (title, author, playerEmail), then GET /api/v1/scores
  L1-CLO8  Demonstrate the risk of authentication without authorization
    ·       how: DELETE a game WITHOUT logging in - it succeeds, and that is the lesson of Level 1

